        "speaker": "client",
        "text": "Hi,\n\nThank you for sending over the updated report design. The overall direction is much stronger now, and I'm happy with the general look and feel, so I do not want to redesign it from scratch.\n\nI would like to make a final round of refinements to improve readability, consistency, and the overall commercial finish before I sign it off.\n\nThe main changes I'd like are:\n\n1\\. Make the front-page score more dominant.\n\nPlease make the \"67/100\" score slightly larger and give it more breathing room so it feels more like the main dashboard result. The customer should immediately notice the score and risk outcome when they open the report.\n\n2\\. Rename \"Security Score\" to \"Vehicle Security Score\"\n\nOn the front page, please change the heading from \"Security Score\" to \"Vehicle Security Score\" to make it feel more complete and professional.\n\n3\\. Simplify the \"What Caused This Result\" section.\n\nThe wording is good, but the dark blue panel currently feels quite text-heavy. Please reduce this section into shorter, easier-to-scan bullet points. For example:\n\n\\- No independent immobilisation\n\\- No circular steering lock\n\\- No live-location tracking\n\\- Storage location is being overvalued\n\\- Owner security habits reduce protection\n\nThe longer explanation can remain elsewhere in the report if needed. Still, page one should feel more immediate and easy to read.\n\n4\\. Remove placeholder text\n\nPlease remove any placeholder text such as \"Click to enter a date.\" This should either be replaced with the actual assessment date or a clean editable placeholder such as \"\\[Assessment Date\\]\".\n\n5\\. Check report code consistency\n\nPlease check that the report code is consistent throughout. I noticed some areas may show \"AC-47\". This should be \"DX-17\" throughout unless there is a specific reason for using something different.\n\n6\\. Clean up the vehicle group section\n\nThe checkboxes next to Range Rover / Range Rover Sport / Defender make the section feel slightly like a form rather than a completed report. Please either make this a cleaner fixed line, such as:\n\n\"Vehicle Group: Range Rover / Range Rover Sport / Defender\"\n\nor make it customer-specific, for example:\n\n\"Vehicle Assessed: Range Rover Sport\"\n\n7\\. Add a subtle header to pages 2 onwards\n\nThe footer works well, but I'd also like a subtle header across the internal pages for consistency. Something simple would be fine, such as:\n\n\"Vehicle Theft Risk Assessment | DX-17 | Confidential\"\n\nThis should be subtle and not take up too much space.\n\n8\\. Refine the red distribution warning on the final page\n\nI like the idea of the warning section, but the red block currently feels a little too heavy. Please keep the warning, but make it slightly more refined and less visually dominant, while still making it clear that the report is confidential and for limited distribution.\n\nOverall, I'm happy with the design direction. I want this final round to focus on polish, readability, consistency and making the report feel like a premium paid assessment.\n\nPlease let me know if the above changes are clear and when you expect to send the revised version.\n\nThanks"
